**Rule.** The deductible, catastrophic cap and network basis of a **TRICARE Select** line are always those of the tier the enrollment holds on the service date; a line is never cost-shared under a neighbouring tier of the same group or under the other group, and a sponsor's later pay-grade change never re-prices lines already adjudicated for earlier service dates.

## What follows the tier held on the service date

For each of the six tiers - TRICARE Select Active Duty Family Member Group A (E-1 to E-4), Group A (E-5 and Above), Group B (E-1 to E-4), Group B (E-5 and Above), TRICARE Select Retiree Group A and TRICARE Select Retiree Group B - the line takes that tier's own:

- individual deductible;
- family deductible;
- family catastrophic cap;
- network outpatient basis (percent of allowed or fixed copayment).

## Hypothetical illustration

A family moves from TRICARE Select Active Duty Family Member Group B (E-1 to E-4) to Group B (E-5 and Above) from January 1 after a promotion. A line for care on the previous 2025-11-03 keeps the E-1 to E-4 tier's deductibles and cap, even if adjudicated after the move; a line for care on 2026-01-15 takes the E-5 and above tier's figures.
